WARNING: BL21,BW25113,MG1655, do(es) not have null-model parameters, and their p-value calculation will be missing in the prediction.list file.

Here is the procedure to fit those parameters:


The parameters for their null-distribution can be computed this way:
- build models with WIsH for each of the listed genomes that miss the null-parameters,
- run the WIsH prediction of the models against a large set of various phages,
- for every model M, fit (e.g. using maximum likelihood) a normal distribution over the scores of M (in the likelihood.matrix file) obtained on phage genomes that are known not to infect the same genus as M,
- for every model M, add a line to the file negFits.csv with the following format:
M<TAB>Mean<TAB>StandardDeviation

To get the p-values associated to a prediction, you can then run the prediction with the options -b -n negFits.csv
when running a prediction.
